WEBVTT

00:00:01.370 --> 00:00:03.450
<i>Astral.</i>

00:00:03.450 --> 00:00:06.660
<i>I'm so glad I started dueling.</i>

00:00:07.890 --> 00:00:10.860
<i>Even if the way we live or the way we speak differs from each other,</i>

00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:14.860
<i>when you play around with people for a while, you end up becoming friends.</i>

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:18.330
<i>If ya seriously try to to, you'll come to understand each other.</i>

00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:21.150
<i>You'll understand each other's hearts.</i>

00:00:23.270 --> 00:00:25.880
<i>Say, Astral...</i>

00:00:26.610 --> 00:00:30.210
<i>Once you collect the Numbers, what're you gonna do after?</i>

00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:34.150
<i>Once I complete my mission, I will simply return to Astral World.</i>

00:00:34.150 --> 00:00:37.700
<i>R-Right... Guess you got a point.</i>

00:00:37.700 --> 00:00:39.440
<i>So what're ya gonna do after that?</i>

00:00:39.440 --> 00:00:41.920
<i>After that?</i>

00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:44.160
<i>I never considered what I'd do that far into the future.</i>

00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:46.500
<i>What the heck, man?
 You don't got any drive at all!</i>

00:00:46.510 --> 00:00:48.810
<i>Upsie- whoa!</i>

00:00:48.810 --> 00:00:50.850
<i>I'm always thinking about it.</i>

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:53.640
<i>Our future, I mean.</i>

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:56.910
<i>It's totally sparkley and radiant!</i>

00:00:56.910 --> 00:00:58.300
<i>A totally refreshing future!</i>

00:00:58.300 --> 00:01:02.010
<i>I'm gonna show you my future one a' these days, alright?</i>

00:01:02.010 --> 00:01:03.710
<i>Your future...?</i>

00:01:04.930 --> 00:01:10.400
<i>But you might not be here anymore when I get there.</i>

00:01:11.020 --> 00:01:13.990
<i>Yuma... I suppose.</i>

00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:19.900
Yeah! You totally just thought, "This guy's going to be so lonely and weeping like a baby when I leave him," didn't you?!

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:26.440
<i>You big jerk! In that case, I'm definitely not gonna cry!</i>

00:01:27.290 --> 00:01:31.670
<i>When the time comes for us to part ways, I'll Duel you off with a big smile on my face!</i>

00:01:31.720 --> 00:01:34.490
<i>That's a promise!</i>

00:01:36.800 --> 00:01:39.750
<i>I promised Astral that...?</i>

00:01:46.210 --> 00:01:48.410
Yuma's only got 300 Life left...!

00:01:48.410 --> 00:01:50.780
On top of that, on his field...

00:01:50.780 --> 00:01:52.800
...he's got no more Monsters!

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:55.400
But Astral's Hope Roots...

00:01:55.400 --> 00:01:58.070
...still has two more Overlay Units.

00:01:58.070 --> 00:02:01.240
Thanks to the Continuous Trap Card, Overlay Accel,

00:02:01.240 --> 00:02:04.110
Astral can attack him once again.

00:02:04.110 --> 00:02:06.910
And if that happens, Yuma will...

00:02:06.910 --> 00:02:09.310
He said before...

00:02:09.550 --> 00:02:14.920
<i>I will fulfill the pact we signed together!</i>

00:02:15.090 --> 00:02:17.390
Could you have meant back then...?

00:02:17.390 --> 00:02:22.280
Here I come, Yuma! I activate the effect of Overlay Accel!

00:02:22.280 --> 00:02:24.750
By detaching one Overlay Unit,

00:02:24.750 --> 00:02:27.060
it can attack once again!

00:02:28.370 --> 00:02:33.350
<i>I said I'd smile during the final Duel we had together before we parted ways.</i>

00:02:33.950 --> 00:02:37.070
Go and attack Yuma directly!

00:02:37.070 --> 00:02:39.280
<i>Smile during our Duel...?</i>

00:02:39.410 --> 00:02:44.580
<i>Duels are supposed to be heart-throbbing, exciting, and fun!</i>

00:02:44.580 --> 00:02:46.880
<i>Yet, I...</i>

00:02:46.880 --> 00:02:49.870
<i>I've been doing nothing but crying!</i>

00:02:49.870 --> 00:02:52.540
<i>Did I lose it along the way?</i>

00:02:52.790 --> 00:02:54.790
<i>Laughing from the bottom of my heart?</i>

00:02:55.540 --> 00:02:58.930
<i>He's been tryin' to make me remember...?</i>

00:02:58.930 --> 00:03:00.600
<i>That little jerk!</i>

00:03:01.220 --> 00:03:04.230
Trap, activate! Must-die Draw!

00:03:04.870 --> 00:03:09.670
When I receive a Direct Attack by a Monster with more Attack Points than my Life Points...

00:03:09.670 --> 00:03:13.390
I draw a card, and if it's a Trap Card,

00:03:13.390 --> 00:03:15.950
the battle is negated and I can activate that card!

00:03:15.950 --> 00:03:19.550
Astral, I remember now! The promise I made to you!

00:03:19.700 --> 00:03:20.930
I see...

00:03:20.930 --> 00:03:24.550
Even so, in order to keep from hurting me...!

00:03:25.840 --> 00:03:28.190
You really suck at bullshitting and being damn serious, ya know that?!

00:03:28.190 --> 00:03:29.740
Yuma...

00:03:30.280 --> 00:03:32.910
I understand our pact now, Astral!

00:03:32.910 --> 00:03:36.720
I'll beat you, laughing from the bottom of my heart!

00:03:36.720 --> 00:03:41.110
I'll show you my future!

00:03:43.240 --> 00:03:45.540
That light...! It couldn't...!

00:03:45.540 --> 00:03:48.730
The Duels of the strongest Duelists are ordained by inevitability!

00:03:48.730 --> 00:03:51.900
Even the cards drawn are decided by the Duelist himself!

00:03:51.900 --> 00:03:55.540
Shining Draw!!

00:03:55.540 --> 00:03:58.240
Yuma, as I thought, you're...

00:03:58.240 --> 00:04:04.240
...no doubt a piece of myself that I lost in that battle so long ago...!

00:04:04.380 --> 00:04:06.530
<i>The other me...</i>

00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:12.220
And what I drew was a Trap Card!

00:04:12.220 --> 00:04:15.590
So the battle's negated!

00:04:15.590 --> 00:04:20.240
And I activate this Trap Card, Master Piece!

00:04:20.240 --> 00:04:26.080
I can Xyz Summon using the two Monsters sent to the Graveyard during this turn!

00:04:26.080 --> 00:04:29.970
I Overlay Gagaga Gunman and Gagaga Samurai!

00:04:29.970 --> 00:04:33.740
Xyz Summon!

00:04:33.740 --> 00:04:37.160
Now's the time to show yourself, Future Number 0!

00:04:38.650 --> 00:04:44.080
Pegasus, now's the time to be set free and fly off toward the future of mankind!

00:04:44.080 --> 00:04:48.470
This is my creation of Heaven and Earth! My future!

00:04:53.560 --> 00:04:56.650
I'm gonna bring it to 'em!

00:04:56.650 --> 00:04:59.650
King of the Future Hope!

00:05:03.720 --> 00:05:06.160
A Rank 0 Number?

00:05:06.560 --> 00:05:09.090
Yuma played a new Number!

00:05:09.090 --> 00:05:11.030
Future Hope...

00:05:11.030 --> 00:05:13.700
It kinda looks like Yuma!

00:05:15.700 --> 00:05:18.020
So this is your future...

00:05:18.740 --> 00:05:22.370
My future still ain't decided yet!

00:05:22.370 --> 00:05:24.540
That's the potential of a Rank 0!

00:05:24.690 --> 00:05:27.580
It's a Number truly just like you.

00:05:27.580 --> 00:05:34.370
Yeah! Astral, I'm gonna enjoy this final Duel with you and enjoy it some more,

00:05:34.370 --> 00:05:36.420
and do it all with a smile 'til the end!

00:05:36.720 --> 00:05:38.740
Come, Yuma!

00:05:38.740 --> 00:05:41.810
I will now end my turn with that!

00:05:41.810 --> 00:05:43.690
Heck yeah! Here goes!

00:05:43.690 --> 00:05:45.760
My turn! Draw!

00:05:45.760 --> 00:05:50.060
I use Future Hope to attack Hope Roots!

00:05:52.040 --> 00:05:58.060
You're having the zero Attack Power Future Hope attack the 2000 Attack Power Hope Roots?!

00:05:58.220 --> 00:06:00.480
You must be planning something, Yuma!

00:06:00.540 --> 00:06:02.610
Who knows! Maybe!

00:06:03.160 --> 00:06:05.110
Is this another bluff?

00:06:07.370 --> 00:06:10.570
I activate Hope Root's effect!

00:06:10.570 --> 00:06:12.570
When it battles an Xyz Monster,

00:06:12.570 --> 00:06:15.740
by giving one of its Overlay Units to the opponent,

00:06:15.740 --> 00:06:20.030
Hope Root's Attack Power, until the end of this turn,

00:06:20.030 --> 00:06:22.950
is the difference between the Monster's Ranks multiplied by 100

00:06:22.950 --> 00:06:26.000
and multiplied by the difference of the opposing Overlay Units!

00:06:26.450 --> 00:06:29.450
This, Hope Root's Attack Power becomes 300!

00:06:31.380 --> 00:06:34.710
I activate King of the Future Hope's effect!

00:06:35.750 --> 00:06:40.030
This card isn't destroyed by battle and all Battle Damage I receive is zero,

00:06:40.030 --> 00:06:43.420
and also, control of the attacking Monster...

00:06:43.420 --> 00:06:45.220
...becomes mine until the end of the battle!

00:06:45.220 --> 00:06:46.020
What?!

00:06:46.470 --> 00:06:49.230
Go, Future Hope!

00:06:49.230 --> 00:06:52.030
Hope Sword Future Slash!!

00:06:56.880 --> 00:07:00.540
Now I've got control of Hope Roots!

00:07:00.540 --> 00:07:02.970
So this is Hope's power of the future!

00:07:03.110 --> 00:07:08.410
Go, Hope Roots! Direct Attack Astral!

00:07:12.420 --> 00:07:13.850
Pretty good, Yuma!

00:07:15.250 --> 00:07:18.390
I set one card face-down and end my turn!

00:07:18.960 --> 00:07:22.580
Looks like your attack wasn't a bluff after all.

00:07:22.580 --> 00:07:24.880
That's the Astral I know!

00:07:24.880 --> 00:07:28.400
You went and lowered Hope Root's Attack Points!

00:07:28.400 --> 00:07:34.070
If you actually found a possibility for the future, I knew there was no way it could be a bluff.

00:07:35.470 --> 00:07:39.210
Dueling with you's the most exciting thing ever!

00:07:39.860 --> 00:07:41.910
Now bring it, Astral!

00:07:41.910 --> 00:07:45.530
Show me your full strength!

00:07:45.530 --> 00:07:48.590
This is starting to turn into quite the amazing Duel!

00:07:48.590 --> 00:07:49.490
Yeah.

00:07:49.490 --> 00:07:51.920
Neither one's giving an inch!

00:07:51.960 --> 00:07:55.580
But Yuma and Astral both seem to be having fun!

00:07:55.620 --> 00:07:59.460
Yuma, if your Rank 0 is the potential of the future,

00:07:59.460 --> 00:08:02.870
then I shall rise even higher than that!

00:08:02.870 --> 00:08:05.070
All light shall become my power!

00:08:05.070 --> 00:08:08.450
All hope and aspiration radiates within my right hand!

00:08:09.090 --> 00:08:11.090
Shining Draw!!

00:08:13.090 --> 00:08:14.640
It's here, Yuma.

00:08:14.640 --> 00:08:19.580
I activate the Hyper-Rank-Up Magic, Ultimate Force!

00:08:20.030 --> 00:08:24.970
As long a Hope is on my field, it Ranks Up a Rank 10 or higher Number,

00:08:24.970 --> 00:08:27.390
and uses this card as an Overlay Unit!

00:08:27.420 --> 00:08:30.630
Rank-Up! Hyper Xyz Change!

00:08:30.630 --> 00:08:34.060
Appear before us, Number 99!

00:08:35.360 --> 00:08:38.370
Memories of my soul that were split apart!

00:08:38.370 --> 00:08:44.040
Now joining together as one united star, the Will of God pierces though the sky like thunder!

00:08:44.420 --> 00:08:48.400
This is now the final destination at the top of all Numbers!

00:08:48.400 --> 00:08:52.000
Dragon King of Wishes - Hope Dragoon!

00:08:57.140 --> 00:09:00.350
So that's the Rank 10 Number 99...

00:09:00.350 --> 00:09:03.270
Dragon King of Wishes, Hope Dragoon...

00:09:02.350 --> 00:09:07.020
<i>"Our Bonds Forever... Let's All Bring it to 'Em!!"</i>

00:09:03.310 --> 00:09:07.400
Here I come! I activate Hope Dragoon's effect!

00:09:07.400 --> 00:09:10.900
Once per turn, it targets one Number in the Graveyard,

00:09:10.900 --> 00:09:13.490
and Special Summons it with its effects negated!

00:09:14.400 --> 00:09:17.780
Be reborn! Number 39!

00:09:17.780 --> 00:09:21.240
King of Wishes, Beyond the Hope!

00:09:22.120 --> 00:09:23.410
He even brought Beyond...

00:09:23.410 --> 00:09:25.960
But Future Hope's effect will-

00:09:25.960 --> 00:09:27.120
Are you sure about that?!

00:09:27.120 --> 00:09:28.170
What?!

00:09:28.170 --> 00:09:33.130
I use Hope Dragoon to attack Future Hope!

00:09:33.510 --> 00:09:34.380
No you don't!

00:09:34.720 --> 00:09:37.720
I activate Future Hope's effect once again!

00:09:38.510 --> 00:09:42.560
It can't be destroyed in battle and all Battle Damage is reduced to zero!

00:09:42.560 --> 00:09:46.850
I then gain control of the battling Monster!

00:09:47.310 --> 00:09:51.570
It won't be that easy!
 Hope Dragoon's other effect activates!

00:09:51.860 --> 00:09:55.110
When this Monster leaves my field,

00:09:55.110 --> 00:09:57.570
by detaching one Overlay Unit...

00:09:58.450 --> 00:10:00.530
That effect is negated!

00:10:00.530 --> 00:10:04.200
And all Monsters other than Hope Dragoon are destroyed!

00:10:04.200 --> 00:10:05.660
Say what?!

00:10:17.130 --> 00:10:18.300
I won't let you get away with it!

00:10:18.300 --> 00:10:20.720
I activate Future Hope's effect!

00:10:21.050 --> 00:10:22.810
By detaching one Overlay Unit,

00:10:22.810 --> 00:10:25.850
I negate this card's destruction!

00:10:27.430 --> 00:10:30.810
So you can't destroy my Future Hope!

00:10:32.270 --> 00:10:34.440
But that is not what I was aiming for!

00:10:34.440 --> 00:10:35.530
What!?

00:10:35.860 --> 00:10:39.490
The one I'm destroying is Beyond the Hope!

00:10:39.950 --> 00:10:44.410
And the Attack Points of the destroyed Monster are given to you as damage!

00:10:45.910 --> 00:10:47.370
No way!

00:10:47.370 --> 00:10:50.830
The destroyed Beyond the Hope had 3000 Attack Points!

00:10:51.790 --> 00:10:54.170
If he gets hit with that, Yuma will...!

00:11:03.010 --> 00:11:04.850
NO!!

00:11:06.020 --> 00:11:09.270
I activate Future Hope's other effect!

00:11:13.690 --> 00:11:15.730
By detaching one Overlay Unit,

00:11:15.730 --> 00:11:20.200
all Effect Damage I take is negated!

00:11:22.280 --> 00:11:23.160
Whew!

00:11:23.160 --> 00:11:25.700
I will now end my turn with that.

00:11:27.410 --> 00:11:28.700
Not too shabby, Yuma!

00:11:30.580 --> 00:11:33.630
Now this is what I call a final Duel with you...

00:11:34.500 --> 00:11:36.300
And I ain't gonna let it end so quickly!

00:11:36.300 --> 00:11:38.170
I'm a bit envious of them!

00:11:38.170 --> 00:11:39.420
Yeah!

00:11:39.420 --> 00:11:41.720
They're enjoying this Duel from the bottom of their hearts.

00:11:42.760 --> 00:11:44.390
They don't need words.

00:11:44.390 --> 00:11:47.720
Yeah, they're speaking to each other as they clash souls against one another!

00:11:47.720 --> 00:11:49.180
Now this is what I call a Duel!

00:11:49.180 --> 00:11:50.980
That's just like those two!

00:11:50.980 --> 00:11:51.850
Yeah!

00:11:51.850 --> 00:11:54.610
They're almost starting to shine, cat!

00:11:55.110 --> 00:11:58.900
<i>This will likely be the final turn... I...</i>

00:11:59.280 --> 00:12:00.240
<i>Astral...</i>

00:12:00.320 --> 00:12:01.820
Okay, let's do this!

00:12:02.320 --> 00:12:04.070
My turn!

00:12:06.700 --> 00:12:10.120
I'm gonna bring it to ya!

00:12:10.410 --> 00:12:13.420
DRAW!!

00:12:16.130 --> 00:12:20.210
Astral... I'm gonna give this my all!

00:12:20.840 --> 00:12:22.470
Bring it! Yuma!

00:12:22.760 --> 00:12:26.430
I use Future Hope to attack Hope Dragoon!

00:12:27.050 --> 00:12:30.350
I'm gonna gain control of your Monster!

00:12:30.520 --> 00:12:34.020
It's useless! I activate Hope Dragoon's effect!

00:12:34.020 --> 00:12:37.440
It negates the effect that removes it from the field,

00:12:37.900 --> 00:12:40.530
and it destroys Future Hope!

00:12:40.820 --> 00:12:43.450
I activate Future Hope's effect!

00:12:43.780 --> 00:12:47.320
I detach one Overlay Unit and negate his destruction!

00:12:49.330 --> 00:12:51.660
Heh! The real fight starts now!

00:12:51.700 --> 00:12:55.040
Trap, activate! Bring it to 'Em Challenge!

00:12:55.040 --> 00:12:57.130
During my turn's Battle Phase,

00:12:57.130 --> 00:13:00.460
it negates the effect of one Xyz Monster being attacked...

00:13:00.460 --> 00:13:03.470
...and allows it to attack once again!

00:13:03.510 --> 00:13:06.340
Impossible! If he negates the Hope's effect...!

00:13:06.340 --> 00:13:08.390
He'll be destroyed in the battle!

00:13:08.390 --> 00:13:10.680
I then activate another Trap!

00:13:10.680 --> 00:13:12.680
Braving Memory!

00:13:12.850 --> 00:13:14.940
When two Numbers battle,

00:13:15.060 --> 00:13:17.940
for every Number in either player's Graveyard,

00:13:17.940 --> 00:13:23.690
Future Hope gains 500 Attack Points during the battle!

00:13:23.690 --> 00:13:27.360
Thus, its Attack Points raise to 4000!

00:13:30.780 --> 00:13:35.660
Awesome! It's Hope and Shark's and Kaito's Numbers!

00:13:35.710 --> 00:13:38.670
But its Attack Power's the same as Hope Dragoon!

00:13:38.670 --> 00:13:40.500
So they'll destroy each other?!

00:13:40.670 --> 00:13:44.170
I activate Braving Memory's other effect!

00:13:44.210 --> 00:13:48.180
My Monsters can't be destroyed in battle during this turn!

00:13:48.180 --> 00:13:51.010
Then, when the opponent's Monster is destroyed,

00:13:51.010 --> 00:13:53.770
and they don't take damage,

00:13:53.770 --> 00:13:56.850
they can battle once again!

00:14:10.570 --> 00:14:15.040
<i>Astral... When this next attack hits, I'll...</i>

00:14:16.870 --> 00:14:21.540
I'll attack directly with Future Hope!!

00:14:21.540 --> 00:14:22.960
It's not over yet!

00:14:22.960 --> 00:14:26.470
I activate the Continuous Trap, The Door of Destiny!

00:14:28.880 --> 00:14:30.840
The Door of Destiny?!

00:14:38.190 --> 00:14:40.230
Th-This place...!

00:14:40.230 --> 00:14:42.770
The Continuous Trap, The Door of Destiny.

00:14:42.770 --> 00:14:46.990
It negates a Direct Attack and Special Summons this card.

00:14:46.990 --> 00:14:50.410
And during my next turn, I can Banish any Numbers from the Graveyard,

00:14:50.410 --> 00:14:55.620
dealing 500 points of damage to my opponent for each.

00:14:56.120 --> 00:14:59.540
Unless you manage to destroy this door, you lose.

00:14:59.580 --> 00:15:03.000
It's because of this door that I met you...

00:15:03.590 --> 00:15:06.670
It's where everything began for us.

00:15:09.380 --> 00:15:12.680
That's right! Back when I first saw this door...!

00:15:12.680 --> 00:15:17.980
<i>He who opens this door shall obtain a new power.</i>

00:15:17.980 --> 00:15:21.230
<i>However, as the price for this power...</i>

00:15:21.230 --> 00:15:24.480
<i>...you shall lose that which is most important to you.</i>

00:15:24.690 --> 00:15:27.400
Astral... I see now!

00:15:28.240 --> 00:15:31.200
The thing that's most important to me... It's...

00:15:32.110 --> 00:15:34.780
It has to be you!

00:15:34.780 --> 00:15:36.790
But I don't want you to...!

00:15:36.790 --> 00:15:37.790
Do not be afraid!

00:15:38.750 --> 00:15:39.870
Astral!

00:15:40.410 --> 00:15:44.630
I know that you're still holding something in your hand.

00:15:45.130 --> 00:15:47.960
Use that hand to open up the future!

00:15:47.960 --> 00:15:51.430
No not fear the future, Yuma!

00:15:51.430 --> 00:15:54.180
Astral, could you be...?

00:15:54.340 --> 00:15:58.060
In order to give me the courage to leave you...!

00:15:58.060 --> 00:16:02.730
You're a hundred years too early to challenge me to a Duel!

00:16:02.730 --> 00:16:04.350
Astral...

00:16:07.110 --> 00:16:12.450
Here I come! I activate the Quick-Play Magic, Double-Up Chance!

00:16:12.450 --> 00:16:15.280
When a Monster's attack is negated,

00:16:15.280 --> 00:16:20.580
its Attack Power is doubled and it can attack again!

00:16:20.580 --> 00:16:23.460
Come, Future Hope!

00:16:27.880 --> 00:16:31.340
This is my true, final attack!

00:16:31.340 --> 00:16:33.760
Now, come! Yuma!

00:16:33.760 --> 00:16:36.220
Here goes, Astral!

00:16:36.220 --> 00:16:39.640
<i>Astral... I won't ever forget...</i>

00:16:40.180 --> 00:16:45.400
The times we spent fighting together, crying together, laughing together, fighting each other, and making up...

00:16:45.400 --> 00:16:52.190
<i>Because you were always there by my side.</i>

00:16:52.190 --> 00:16:53.740
<i>But from here on out...</i>

00:16:56.370 --> 00:16:58.950
I'm gonna bring it to 'em!

00:16:58.950 --> 00:17:04.580
I'm gonna cut open a path to the future!
 Hope Sword Future Slash!!

00:17:36.740 --> 00:17:38.490
Astral.

00:17:44.080 --> 00:17:46.460
That was splendid, Yuma.

00:17:46.460 --> 00:17:47.330
Yeah.

00:17:51.300 --> 00:17:55.880
That's... the Numeron Code.

00:17:58.430 --> 00:18:01.100
It would seem the time has come for us to part ways.

00:18:01.100 --> 00:18:02.640
Astral.

00:18:02.640 --> 00:18:04.140
Yuma.

00:18:05.100 --> 00:18:08.520
I got it! I definitely ain't gonna cry!

00:18:08.520 --> 00:18:12.190
I loved that smile of yours.

00:18:12.190 --> 00:18:16.150
I hope to never forget that smile.

00:18:16.570 --> 00:18:18.160
Bring it to 'em.

00:18:23.830 --> 00:18:26.120
Astral!

00:18:26.120 --> 00:18:32.040
Bring it to 'em! And bring out your courage and take a step forward!

00:18:32.040 --> 00:18:36.090
So that, no matter what pinch you're in, you never give up!

00:18:36.090 --> 00:18:39.510
So you'll take up endless challenges!

00:18:39.510 --> 00:18:42.970
Thank you, Astral.

00:18:46.890 --> 00:18:55.110
I'll never forget...about you!
 I won't ever forget!

00:18:55.480 --> 00:18:59.700
I, too, will never forget, Yuma!

00:19:03.990 --> 00:19:05.950
Astral!

00:19:05.950 --> 00:19:09.080
ASTRAL!

00:19:13.840 --> 00:19:16.710
Oh, crap! Oh, crap!

00:19:16.800 --> 00:19:18.550
I'm late! Late!

00:19:18.550 --> 00:19:20.880
I'm goin' on ahead!

00:19:21.430 --> 00:19:23.050
Wait up, Tetsuo!

00:19:23.350 --> 00:19:24.760
Like heck I'm gonna wait!

00:19:23.350 --> 00:19:28.520
<i>And just like that, my battle ended and my normal life returned.</i>

00:19:24.760 --> 00:19:26.890
I ain't gonna lose to you today!

00:19:26.890 --> 00:19:28.520
No, I'm gonna win!

00:19:28.520 --> 00:19:31.980
<i>But there was one thing that wasn't the same as before...</i>

00:19:32.350 --> 00:19:34.690
N-No way!

00:19:34.730 --> 00:19:37.190
Unfortunately for you, you're out!

00:19:37.190 --> 00:19:40.610
As punishment, you get to clean the restrooms for one week.

00:19:40.610 --> 00:19:43.240
Shark Sis, anything but that!

00:19:43.240 --> 00:19:45.410
Okay, it's been decided you get <i>two weeks</i>!

00:19:45.410 --> 00:19:50.370
<i>That's right. Astral used the Numeron Code.</i>

00:19:50.370 --> 00:19:55.290
<i>And he brought the Seven Barian Emperors back into the human world as humans.</i>

00:19:57.210 --> 00:20:00.670
That idiot's the same as always.

00:20:00.670 --> 00:20:02.510
<i>And that's not all.</i>

00:20:02.590 --> 00:20:06.560
<i>He also brought back my dad from the Astral World.</i>

00:20:06.560 --> 00:20:09.220
<i>And my mom as well.</i>

00:20:11.100 --> 00:20:13.900
<i>Naturally, Kaito and Orbital returned as well.</i>

00:20:13.900 --> 00:20:17.570
Orbital, analyze this data immediately.

00:20:17.570 --> 00:20:19.070
As you command!

00:20:19.070 --> 00:20:20.490
- As you command!
 - As you command!

00:20:20.490 --> 00:20:22.950
As you command, Big Brother!

00:20:22.990 --> 00:20:25.570
<i>They were now working with Tron and the others...</i>

00:20:25.570 --> 00:20:29.330
<i>studying a way to reopen the door to the Parallel Worlds.</i>

00:20:30.500 --> 00:20:34.960
<i>Right, I just kept on noisily making a ruckus with the guys and Dueling,</i>

00:20:34.960 --> 00:20:39.500
<i>so I guess you really could say that my normal life returned.</i>

00:20:41.090 --> 00:20:45.050
<i>There's just one guy I wish could be...</i>

00:20:47.850 --> 00:20:49.890
<i>...to see everything back to normal.</i>

00:20:56.270 --> 00:20:59.400
This...! Could it be...?!

00:20:59.480 --> 00:21:00.440
Yuma!

00:21:03.280 --> 00:21:04.860
Shark! Kaito!

00:21:04.860 --> 00:21:06.320
Everyone!

00:21:08.120 --> 00:21:10.240
How long're you going to keep sulking for?

00:21:10.240 --> 00:21:11.660
Let's get moving!

00:21:12.120 --> 00:21:15.620
There's a new danger threatening the Astral World.

00:21:15.620 --> 00:21:18.750
What'd you say?! Astral's in trouble?!

00:21:20.500 --> 00:21:23.720
Something has begun gathering the power of Chaos.

00:21:23.720 --> 00:21:25.970
Using the power of the Numeron Code,

00:21:26.180 --> 00:21:29.470
Astral united the Astral World and Barian World as one.

00:21:29.470 --> 00:21:31.680
And we accepted Chaos.

00:21:31.680 --> 00:21:34.980
However, that has instead lead us to a new battle...

00:21:35.850 --> 00:21:38.270
Are you going, Astral?

00:21:38.270 --> 00:21:39.730
Yes.

00:21:40.400 --> 00:21:45.490
W-W-Wait a minute, Yuma! Hold on a minute!

00:21:43.320 --> 00:21:46.450
Whether it's rainy, or windy,
 or a cold winter blizzard, or the burning sun,

00:21:45.950 --> 00:21:49.200
We owe that guy a massive debt.

00:21:46.450 --> 00:21:49.740
<i>they're all ingredients to color each day. 
Don't lose heart, will or love.</i>

00:21:49.200 --> 00:21:52.370
The time has come for all of us to combine our power together!

00:21:49.740 --> 00:21:52.990
<i>The kindness you gave me was strict,
 when we clashed I learned irritation.</i>

00:21:52.370 --> 00:21:55.370
Preparations for the door to the Parallel Worlds are already complete.

00:21:52.990 --> 00:21:57.830
<i>It starts by recognizing our differences, dancing freely,
 the creation of Heaven and Earth.</i>

00:21:55.370 --> 00:21:57.830
Bring it to them, Kaito-<i>sama</i>!

00:21:57.830 --> 00:22:01.250
It is now time for us to move out!

00:21:58.960 --> 00:22:05.010
<i>The truth is, I was lonely. Until I met you.</i>

00:22:01.250 --> 00:22:04.880
I'll show them a nice helping of my fanservice!

00:22:04.880 --> 00:22:07.680
I'll fight alongside Yuma anywhere!

00:22:05.010 --> 00:22:10.800
<i>I lied to myself that being alone was easier.</i>

00:22:07.680 --> 00:22:11.640
We'll unleash the power of the bond our family shares!

00:22:10.800 --> 00:22:17.230
<i>My favorite books and hobbies,
 they don't seem to match.</i>

00:22:11.640 --> 00:22:14.600
Let's draw out the power of us reunited Seven Barian Emperors!

00:22:14.600 --> 00:22:16.850
And use it to fight for Astral!

00:22:16.850 --> 00:22:20.440
I'll let them taste a true Dragon Tamer's Duel!

00:22:17.230 --> 00:22:21.770
<i>You were the only one to nod in agreement with me.</i>

00:22:21.570 --> 00:22:23.230
Now we're talkin'!

00:22:21.770 --> 00:22:24.570
<i>Happiness and sadness and anger and
 Do and Re and Mi and Fa and So and La and Ti and Do,</i>

00:22:23.230 --> 00:22:25.530
I'm gettin' fired up! Raaawr!

00:22:24.570 --> 00:22:26.950
<i>It doesn't work unless they're different,
 the harmony and the scenario.</i>

00:22:25.530 --> 00:22:28.950
Heck yeah! It's been so long since we went wild!

00:22:26.950 --> 00:22:30.240
<i>No one is exactly the same,</i>

00:22:28.950 --> 00:22:30.120
Everyone!

00:22:30.120 --> 00:22:31.870
Ta-da-daaa!

00:22:30.240 --> 00:22:34.450
<i>because that's the reason for living.</i>

00:22:31.870 --> 00:22:35.410
I though it'd be for the best if I gave you a hand with good intentions!

00:22:34.450 --> 00:22:39.920
<i>Even if the sounds are dissonant from time to time,</i>

00:22:35.410 --> 00:22:36.580
Y-You...!

00:22:36.870 --> 00:22:40.750
My, oh my, Vector. Please <i>do</i> behave yourself this time.

00:22:39.920 --> 00:22:45.960
<i>don't give up on the strength that will get you through.</i>

00:22:40.750 --> 00:22:45.170
Maybe, maybe not. But I don't mind going wild with you guys.

00:22:45.630 --> 00:22:48.340
Heck yeah! Now everyone's together!

00:22:45.960 --> 00:22:49.300
<i>When we reach the edge of the world,</i>

00:22:48.340 --> 00:22:52.430
Anyone, good or bad hearts, can fight one another.

00:22:49.300 --> 00:22:53.260
<i>the view we see will be the truth.</i>

00:22:52.430 --> 00:22:55.640
But if you can escape from that borderline,

00:22:53.260 --> 00:22:56.020
<i>Whether it's rainy, or windy,
 or a cold winter blizzard, or the burning sun,</i>

00:22:55.640 --> 00:22:57.980
anyone can get along with each other.

00:22:56.020 --> 00:22:59.140
<i>They're all ingredients to color each day.
 Don't lose heart, will or love.</i>

00:22:57.980 --> 00:23:01.400
Yuma, I shall continue to fight on!

00:22:59.140 --> 00:23:02.440
<i>the kindness you gave me was strict,
 when we clashed I learned irritation.</i>

00:23:01.900 --> 00:23:05.150
Until the day everyone can get along!

00:23:02.440 --> 00:23:07.610
<i>It starts by recognizing our differences, dancing freely,
 the creation of Heaven and Earth.</i>

00:23:07.860 --> 00:23:08.740
Yuma!

00:23:08.740 --> 00:23:09.740
Huh?

00:23:09.740 --> 00:23:13.410
I love you and that smile of yours, Yuma!

00:23:13.410 --> 00:23:14.080
Eh?

00:23:14.330 --> 00:23:15.080
H-Huh?!

00:23:15.080 --> 00:23:17.830
So, we're gonna go get him back, right?

00:23:17.830 --> 00:23:20.040
The person most important to you!

00:23:20.870 --> 00:23:21.790
Yeah!

00:23:21.880 --> 00:23:25.550
This is how I bring it to 'em!

00:23:27.460 --> 00:23:29.470
Wait for me, Astral!

00:23:29.470 --> 00:23:30.930
Let's move out, everyone!

00:23:31.380 --> 00:23:36.430
I'm gonna bring it to 'em!!
